    "chunk_text": "UK gas prices surge by 140%, highest level since 2023\n\nUK wholesale gas prices have surged to 171.34 pence per therm ($ 2.29) as the Israeli-US war on Iran creates havoc in global energy flows.\n\nSince the war on Iran began on February 28, wholesale gas has jumped by about 140% in the UK from 71.13 pence per therm ($ 1.33).\n\nMissile strikes have set parts of Qatar\u2019s Ras Laffan LNG complex ablaze, damaging one of the world\u2019s largest gas hubs.\n\nThe UK remains heavily dependent on imported energy, particularly gas from the Middle East and Qatar."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
