    "description": "Germany says it will act in Middle East only \u2018once the guns fall silent\u2019",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Germany-says-it-will-act-in-Middle-East-only-once-the-guns-fall-silent/56-789816",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1773972127.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-20-dailyftlk-b5fed878-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8c06c833e5a7ffe5d3f46f4cd319073a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 751,
    "chunk_text": "Germany says it will act in Middle East only \u2018once the guns fall silent\u2019\n\nGermany\u2019s Chancellor says Berlin will not intervene in the Middle East while the US-Israel war on Iran continues.\n\nSpeaking in Brussels, Friedrich Merz said Germany\u2019s role would depend on a halt in hostilities.\n\n\u201cWe can and will only be able to get involved once the guns fall silent,\u201d Merz told reporters.\n\n\u201cWe can do a great deal, including opening up the sea lanes and keeping them clear,\u201d he said. \u201cBut we don\u2019t do that while hostilities are ongoing. We\u2019ll only do that once hostilities have ended.\u201d\n\nTrump has lashed out at European countries, saying they have failed to help the US manage the fallout from a war many EU countries consider illegal."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-20-dailyftlk-1ffebfe4",
    "num": "dailyftlk-1ffebfe4",
    "date_str": "2026-03-20",
    "description": "America has lost control of its own foreign policy: Omani Foreign Minister",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/America-has-lost-control-of-its-own-foreign-policy-Omani-Foreign-Minister/56-789817",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1773972151.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-03-20-dailyftlk-1ffebfe4-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ba4f797e89312da959712abf6b5703dc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1285,
    "chunk_text": "America has lost control of its own foreign policy: Omani Foreign Minister\n\nOman\u2019s Foreign Minister Badr Albusaidi, in an op-ed in The Economist, warns that \u201cAmerica has lost control of its own foreign policy\u201d, saying Washington\u2019s allies should help extricate it \u201cfrom this unwanted entanglement\u201d.\n\n\u201cTwice in nine months the United States and Iran have been on the verge of a real deal,\u201d said Albusaidi.\n\n\u201cIt was a shock but not a surprise when on February 28th \u2013 just a few hours after the latest and most substantive talks \u2013 Israel and America again launched an unlawful military strike against the peace that had briefly appeared really possible.\u201d\n\nIran\u2019s retaliation against what it claims are American targets on its neighbours was an \u201cinevitable, if deeply regrettable and completely unacceptable, result,\u201d he said.\n\nFor Iran, faced with a war to \u201cterminate the Islamic Republic, this was probably the only rational option available to the Iranian leadership\u201d.\n\n\u201cThe American administration\u2019s greatest miscalculation, of course, was allowing itself to be drawn into this war in the first place. This is not America\u2019s war, and there is no likely scenario in which both Israel and America will get what they want from it,\u201d added Albusaidi."
  },
